{
  "module": "scene",
  "note": "The same argument as showcase-flight-computed.json, on a sphere. Every dot is a real coordinate baked from Natural Earth (core/globe-dots.js, `make globe-dots`); the route is a true great circle, a slerp between JFK and CDG lifted off the surface, never the flat map's quadratic; and the terminator is a HEMISPHERE computed from one sun vector that the land and the sea both read, so they cannot disagree. What a globe earns over the chart is exactly that last part: day and night on a planet is a hemisphere, and a flat map can only ever draw a line where one should be. What it costs is that half the world is behind it. Both films exist so the trade can be seen rather than argued about.",
  "aspect": "16:9",
  "theme": "vawe-dark",
  "duration": 20,
  "destination": "web",
  "audio": {
    "silent": true,
    "_why": "As showcase-flight-computed.json: the film wants a bed that lifts with the light, and shipping the wrong one is worse than shipping none. A gap, stated, not a claim that mute is better."
